Experimental source-owned project-presence retirement; not applied by Context Foundry.
UNQUALIFIED handle-immutability candidate: baseline tests pass, but the final fix
has not been compiled or run because the same-round disk guard refuses launch.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006, bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires prior caller/auth/refusal/restricted/catalog/settings/empty-auth patches.
Modules: launch/presence::{ownStartupDaemonPresence,registerDaemonProjectPresence,
retireStartupDaemonPresence}; main CLI explicit flag and original observer;
sdk::{createAgentSession,retireRestrictedStartupPresence}; CLI args/flag table.
Tests: startup-presence-owner.test.ts; existing daemon-prune/stale-lease, main/CLI,
auth, restricted SDK, caller/settings and empty-auth suites.
Difference: --startup-presence requires --restrict-tools and is selected only by the
explicit startup diagnostic. Keep the real original registration and private file.
One module owner closes registration admission before joining that original, its
completion observer and whichever caller first began original cleanup. Cached
exports and close references retain the same lifecycle. Failed or ambiguous work
cannot produce a receipt. The owned returned handle is frozen before exposure, so callers cannot replace
its original close. Ordinary returned handles retain their existing mutability.
The original close is a shared promise, cancels its
postmortem callback and verifies absence after real removal; partial failed writes
are cleaned. Ordinary registration remains available without the option. The CLI
joins its original logging/catch observer and the SDK binds the exact opaque owner
to the sealed original session/registry after auth retirement. No paths or user data
are returned in settlement metadata. Native baseline RPC EOF leaves its old presence
file; the selected profile removes its file before its retirement receipt.
No daemon server shutdown, global daemon absence, physical FD release, complete
inventory, Ready, paid execution or signing is established. Dated receipts retain
actual native IO, held/error controls and full admission remains HOLD.

